      {
        "id": 95468,
        "name": "JimB",
        "username": "JimB",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jimb/{size}/2093_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-15T15:13:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Katsue\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/48/2012_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Katsue:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Even on normal level, it takes several turns to go through the Underbosses, because you can’t leave any of them out.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You can if Haka is destroying and burying their mooks under Savage Mana.  The Broker, the Deputy, and the Fence become completely irrelevant after you’ve stolen their cards, so you get to just beat up the Contract and the Muscle.</p>\n<p>I admit it’s a pretty specific set of circumstances, though.</p>",
