      {
        "id": 95469,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-15T15:35:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The real threat of the deck is boosted hitmen. &nbsp;Other than that he is managable.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Finding a way to deal with the hitman is key. &nbsp;Lead/evolution/projectile is amazing, you just win. &nbsp;Superhuman will do good as well, and it is one of the few matches where shielding winds is just amazing. &nbsp;Synaptic is great, since Tachyon can avoid taking 3 damage from most other sources. &nbsp;Hairtrigger - Bee bot can stop him, as can reactive/ablative + 1 damage (hairtrigger or a boost) &nbsp;Ra can flame barrier for 3 pretty easily and Wraith with combat also works (those two can hurt you vs. the damage one-shot if it dials your number, cause Chariman hurts)</p><p>My favorite was the most timely fixed point ever making stealth bot indestructible as the chairman played hitman and operative played contract bringing out a 2nd hitman, with damage + (H). &nbsp;We were all pretty pumped about SB's -50hp.</p><p>Alternately close quarters got us killed when Legacy was up front and immune to projectile. &nbsp;That really sucked.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:18.929Z",
