        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-15T17:10:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Katsue\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/48/2012_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Katsue:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>lynkfox wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I actually find the Chairman /easier/ on advanced. Sure he does more damage and takes far less, but he flips far sooner, allowing heroes to wail on him much faster without having to go through as many turns with the thugs/underbosses\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI'm sorry, but the Chairman flipping sooner on advanced is not a good thing. Even on normal level, it takes several turns to go through the Underbosses, because you can't leave any of them out. Every experiment of mine in doing so has been a miserable failure. Hitting the Chairman earlier just means getting hit back, and then seeing him heal all the damage because of the Broker and his one shot.Also, Enforcers become a crippling card lock when he flips, and Hit Man is absolutely devastating if you don't have redirection/immunity, whereas they're annoying but manageable when Chairman's on his front side.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Katsue. It was entirely my opinion. I find damage mitagation and dealing with more damage easier to handle than hordes of minions. Target Priority is a pain in my patooe, so to me, advanced chairman flipping and opening himself up sooner for the big hits (wrathful comes to mind) make the game easier for me. Your milleage may vary.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
