      {
        "id": 95477,
        "name": "Katsue",
        "username": "Katsue",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-19T22:43:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;Katsue. It was entirely my opinion. I find damage mitagation and dealing with more damage easier to handle than hordes of minions. Target Priority is a pain in my patooe, so to me, advanced chairman flipping and opening himself up sooner for the big hits (wrathful comes to mind) make the game easier for me. Your milleage may vary.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You usually can't make the big hits on turn 2, though, because they require setup. Also, you have to kill the Operative as well as the Chairman, so going all-out to kill him and taking loads of hits in the process isn't very helpful, because the rest of the mob will just carry on unhindered.</p>",
        "post_number": 34,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:19.528Z",
